INSERT INTO `page_text` (`ID`,`Text`,`NextPageID`,`PlayerConditionID`,`Flags`,`VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
(223,'Disperse information as you deem necessary.\r\n\r\nTirisfal Regional Command\r\nCaptain Melrose\r\nCaptain Vachon\r\nCaptain Perrine\r\n\r\nDirectives by the order of the Highlord.\r\n\r\nCaptain Perrine, further fortify your position at the southwest tower (as designated). Additional supplies will be dispatched at a later date. In the meantime, materiel should be obtainable from the surrounding farms. Also, further reconnaissance and information',224,0,0,70124),
(224,'should be gathered about the organization of the undead in Brill.\r\n\r\nCaptain Vachon, there appears to be increased movement by the undead near the northern tower. This insurgence must be quickly and decisively dealt with.\r\n\r\nCaptain Melrose, there are concerns about the level of organization of the undead near the borders of the Plaguelands. A fresh group of men will be dispatched to your position in the coming weeks.\r\n\r\nGlory under the Light',0,0,0,70124),
(244,'Lord Bethor Iceshard,\r\n\r\nAs per your instructions, I send to you the agent you requested.  It is the bearer of this note.\r\n\r\nThis person has shown to be dependable and able to follow orders, is proven against the forces of the Scourge, and is my choice for your mission.\r\n\r\nMay She reign supreme,\r\n-Magistrate Sevren\r\n\r\n',0,0,0,70124),
(10322,'The cult hit us by surprise. Raani never saw it coming and Arvensus took a sword to the gut. For my part, I took a lightning bolt to the chest and blacked out. They never bothered to finish me off... I guess they assumed my wounds would do me in. When it\'s all said and done, I suspect they might.',10323,0,0,70124),
(10323,'As soon as the fighting stopped, they started moving massive crates of windstones to the top of the tower. The leader, some kind of priest, said something about a ritual.\r\n\r\nI\'m writing this note just in case I don\'t make it back to Shen\'dar to warn Aonda, but they are doing something here. Something bad.',10324,0,0,70124),
(10324,'If anyone finds this, please, do your best to stop them. There were only a few left at the tower when I scribbled this note and crawled away.\r\n\r\nAlso, try and get Raani\'s lucky feather from his body. He liked to tell tall tales about how he plucked it from some kind of firebird and I think he\'d want to make sure that it made its way back home.\r\n\r\nIf you are also able to retrieve Arvensus Shadowsong\'s family signet from his body, please do so. High Elder Shadowsong is his uncle and he would want it to be returned to the family.',0,0,0,70124),
(10721,'<You touch the small white crystal and you can hear faint sounds on the wind. This is an audio recording of some sort.>\r\n\r\n"An excerpt from the Shal\'nan\'s speech at the groundbreaking ceremony for the Shrine of the Four Winds, Zephras Isle."',10723,0,0,70124),
(10723,'"With the founding of our new home here in the clouds, we embark on a new age of peace and prosperity for our people.\r\n\r\nYou have all endured so much to make it here. I have watched our people grow into a hardy, self-reliant society, which fills me with a pride I cannot hope to describe in full.\r\n\r\nThe greatest part of that pride, however, is that it has become clear to me that I no longer have any need to act as our singular ruler."',10724,0,0,70124),
(10724,'"Thus, I am abdicating my position as your leader and handing over governance of our Skyborne Isles to a carefully chosen council of provincial elders. After the transition period is over, you will have the opportunity to choose your own leaders, and your voices will determine the direction we take from here on. \r\n\r\nYou have demonstrated the ability to lead yourselves better than any king, queen, prince, or other individual sovereign ever could--and that fills me with profound pride."',10725,0,0,70124),
(10725,'"I will continue to serve our people here on Zephras, and I will devote much of my time to furthering our relationship with the wind spirits to whom we owe so much. The elemental spirits are wondrous and wise, and we still have so much to learn from one another.\r\n\r\nI am devoted to seeing the shen\'dorei persevere in this beautiful and strange realm--and to seeing that we do so freely, justly, and unshackled by tyranny."',10726,0,0,70124),
(10726,'"Thank you for everything you\'ve sacrificed, everything you\'ve built, and everything you\'ve taught me about how to be a better person. You all represent the unshakable resolve of the shen\'dorei people. We will thrive in this beautiful new world and reach new heights together."',0,0,0,70124),
(10732,'<You touch the small white crystal and you can hear faint sounds on the wind. This is an audio recording of some sort.>\r\n\r\n"The Rebellion in Eldre\'Thalas, Part 1"',10733,0,0,70124),
(10733,'"In the days immediately following the turmoil at the Well of Eternity, there was much unrest in Eldre\'Thalas. The demonic forces that poured from the Well nearly overwhelmed the beleaguered elvish kingdoms, ravaging the land and killing indiscriminately. If not for the intervention of the demigod Goldrinn and the sacrifice of countless kaldorei heroes, the kingdom of Eldre\'Thalas would surely have been overrun and destroyed."',10734,0,0,70124),
(10734,'"After the climax of the war and the Great Sundering of Kalimdor, the new reality of a world bereft of the sustaining magic on which our people depended quickly became apparent. The ruling house of Eldre\'Thalas--House Tortheldrin--rapidly set plans in motion to ensure stability and continuity of our way of life. However, the methods they intended to employ left many deeply concerned."',10735,0,0,70124),
(10735,'"The young Prince Tortheldrin intended to build a network of crystalline foci and use them to siphon and shape a new font of power for our people to draw upon. The point of contention for many was that he intended to use the very power that nearly destroyed our world to accomplish this. He meant to siphon this power from a demon world within the Twisting Nether itself. \r\n\r\nMany rightly feared this could open a new door through which demonic entities might gain once again access to our world."',0,0,0,70124),
(10736,'<You touch the small white crystal and you can hear faint sounds on the wind. This is an audio recording of some sort.>\r\n\r\n"The Rebellion in Eldre\'Thalas, Part 2"',10737,0,0,70124),
(10737,'"There were those who loudly opposed the Prince\'s plan to channel a font of demonic energy to power his network of crystalline foci. Many of the detractors were members of outspoken noble families who attempted to use their influence to turn public sentiment against House Tortheldrin and the Prince\'s plan."',10738,0,0,70124),
(10738,'"Prince Tortheldrin grew frustrated, fearing that delays and debate would lead to the further deterioration of his kingdom. \r\n\r\nAs a result, his response to this resistance was swift and brutal. Over the course of a single bloody night, a purge was carried out that saw the complete destruction of dozens of noble houses. All who publicly opposed Tortheldrin were abruptly silenced, and entire lineages were destroyed overnight."',10739,0,0,70124),
(10739,'"The terror of such brazen suppression caused a shocked silence to fall over the people of Eldre\'Thalas. All discourse around Prince Tortheldrin\'s plan abruptly ceased... for a time, at least. Unfortunately for the Prince, the harder tyrants squeeze their people, the brighter the flames of resistance burn.\r\n\r\nThere were those who resolved to ensure our people did not repeat Queen Azshara\'s mistakes. A group of scholars formerly of the order of the Shen\'dralar met in secret and formed a pact. Swearing to stop the Prince by any means necessary, they began to plant the seeds of rebellion."',0,0,0,70124),
(10907,'<You touch the small white crystal and you can hear faint sounds on the wind. This is an audio recording of some sort.>\r\n\r\n"The Sky-Touched Mystery"',10908,0,0,70124),
(10908,'"Much of the flora and fauna of the Skyborne Isles has been shaped by the elemental forces that reign here in the realm of Skywall. Many creatures once bound to the earth now bear avian traits such as beaks, talons, and feathers. Others have gained the power of flight, though such transformations remain less common than other outward changes.\r\n\r\nAmong the shen\'dorei, the elemental plane\'s influence upon the body has been gradual and subtle. Yet in recent generations its effects have grown increasingly dramatic. Consider, for instance, the phenomenon now commonly called the "Sky-Touched Blessing."',10909,0,0,70124),
(10909,'"It\'s well documented since our ascent to Skywall that our people have adopted more lithe, slender forms, but this occurred over the course of many millennia. In contrast, the first recorded case of the Sky-Touched Blessing--which causes shen\'dorei children to be born with vivid cerulean skin--was noted fewer than five generations ago.\r\n\r\nWithin a single generation of its first appearance, one child in twenty born among the Skyborne bore this curious alteration. Two generations later, that rate had doubled."',10910,0,0,70124),
(10910,'"Today, three in ten children born on the Skyborne Isles have the striking complexion of the Sky-Touched. In recent centuries, the acceleration of our physical alterations has increased, and many scholars believe that the last vestiges of our kaldorei heritage may vanish entirely within two to three more generations.\r\n\r\nThe cause of this transformation may never be fully understood. Yet it is plain that, in making our lives within the elemental plane, we as a people are being changed by it in turn. Skywall is a realm of wonders, but this serves as a sober reminder that we still know perilously little of what such a place may work upon those not born to it."',0,0,0,70124),
(10911,'<You touch the small white crystal and you can hear faint sounds on the wind. This is an audio recording of some sort.>\r\n\r\n"On The Windlord."',10912,0,0,70124),
(10912,'"Who is Al\'Akir the Windlord? The priests of the radical Al\'Aketh would have us believe him to be the true ruler of Skywall, the realm we now call home. In their telling, we are but interlopers here, and one day Al\'Akir shall appear before us to reckon with our trespass into his dominion within the elemental plane.\r\n\r\nThough such claims may at first seem the ravings of the misguided or the mad, there may yet be some measure of truth in them. When asked of Al\'Akir\'s nature, the wind spirits grow evasive and agitated. Indeed, even the mere speaking of the so-called "Windlord\'s" name appears to cause them profound unease, perhaps even fear."',10913,0,0,70124),
(10913,'"Whatever the truth may be, our benefactors clearly have no wish to speak of Al\'Akir or his servants, and they are quick to dismiss all rumors of the Windlord\'s presence as idle fancy, unworthy of serious heed. They assure us that we need not trouble ourselves with such matters here, safe upon our Skyborne Isles. While this offers solemn comfort to many, it also raises a troubling question: what, precisely, are the wind spirits concealing from us?"',10914,0,0,70124),
(10914,'"Of late, the magisters of the High Order have grown increasingly wary of the wind spirits\' motives, insisting that all powers and perils native to this realm must be better understood. Even if such dangers lie far from us now, the magisters maintain that such knowledge will better prepare us to face whatever may yet come."',10915,0,0,70124),
(10915,'"The skyseer elders among the Windshapers, by contrast, place implicit trust in the wind spirits and regard any questioning of their designs as an affront to our benefactors. They hold that our patrons in Skywall have already sacrificed much to bring us here and sustain us. They assert that if any further knowledge was vital to our survival, they would surely reveal it in due course. This difference in belief has given rise to no small measure of tension between the two orders.\r\n\r\nWhatever the truth may be, it is plain that we are not alone in this realm, and that many mysteries yet remain beyond our present understanding."',0,0,0,70124);
